swap('''Stable drone and event IDs determine processing order, but observations at the same time are assessed together.''','''At a timestamp, first apply and validate scheduled hidden physical changes, then resolve charging interruptions and arrivals, then take all due sensor samples from that resulting physical state, then complete charge/availability and expiry transitions. A qualified fresh observation at the exact expiry instant replaces expiring evidence before eligibility is assessed. Stable IDs break ties within these phases. Observations at the same time are assessed together; hidden physical epoch provenance stays inside the sim and evaluator. Public readings carry only their observed timestamp and the evidence-compatibility epoch established by public reports or observed inconsistency, never a hidden incident ID. When a change becomes known later, retain raw readings and explicitly revise their epoch dispositions instead of pooling incompatible states.''')
insert_before('Each hold has a unique `cycle_id`.', '''A route failure must not suppress an urgent diagnostic finding. After validating a manager response's schema, source and evidence links, publish an immutable `PendingDiagnosticNotice` on a separate public diagnostic channel before attempting route acceptance. It carries the proposed revisions, LLM finding and reason, independently checked recommendation, source cycle and revision, and a clear `PROPOSED_NOT_ACCEPTED` status. The UI shows it immediately beside the raw observation, including any route-blocking reason. This notice does not change accepted hypotheses, topology, tasks, routes or the decision dependency revision, and cannot authorize release. Subsequent notices link acceptance, rejection or supersession without erasing history. Accepted `World.manager_turns` link the corresponding notice. If no manager response is valid, the already-published direct condition diagnostic still shows the measured violation without an invented LLM explanation.
''')
